"In 1900, around 500 km³ of water was used by the agricultural sector around the world. The figures for industrial and domestic water consumption were around one-fifth of that amount. From 1900 to 2000, water use for agriculture increased to around 3,000 km³, industrial water use rose to nearly 1,500 km³, and domestic water consumption reached approximately 500 km³.": "",
"In the year 2000, the populations of Brazil and the Congo were 176 million and 5.2 million, respectively. Similarly, Brazil had far more irrigated land than the Congo, with 26,500 km² and 100 km², respectively. Water consumption per person in Brazil, at 359 m³, was significantly higher than that in the Congo, at only 8 m³.": "",
